1.2  "You" or "Your" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights
     under this License, together with any entity that controls, is controlled
     by, or is under common control with that entity. "Control" means direct or
     indirect ownership of more than fifty percent (50%) of the voting
     interests, or the power to direct the management of the entity.

1.3  "Software" means the Dioreo source code, configuration, scripts,
     documentation, and all other material contained in the repository at
     https://github.com/HarkiratMangat/dioreo, in whole or in part, in
     source or object form, including all past and future versions, and
     including any portion, fragment, module, function, or file of it.

1.4  "Curated Data" means the compilations of factual information assembled,
     selected, arranged, verified, and maintained by or for the Licensor,
     including without limitation the weapon loadout and attachment database,
     the build rankings and badges, the lucky-draw and pricing datasets, the
     seasonal calendar and patch-note records, and the associated descriptive
     text. Curated Data is protected as a compilation and as a database
     independently of any protection attaching to the code that reads it.

1.5  "Brand Assets" means the name "Dioreo", the former name "Dior's Builds",
     the name "dior" as used in
     connection with the Software, any logo, avatar, banner, emoji set, color
     palette, accent-color scheme, message layout, or other element of the
     visual or textual identity of the Software or the Official Service,
     together with any name or mark confusingly similar to any of them.

1.6  "Official Service" means the instance or instances of the Software
     operated by or on behalf of the Licensor and made available to the public
     through Discord, together with any successor, replacement, or additional
     public service operated by the Licensor.

1.7  "Modify" means to adapt, alter, translate, port, refactor, extend,
     abridge, merge with other material, or otherwise create a work based upon
     the Software, and "Modification" means the result of doing so. A
     Modification is a derivative work for the purposes of applicable
     copyright law.

1.8  "Deploy" means to run, execute, host, install, or otherwise make the
     Software or a Modification operational in any circumstance in which any
     person other than You is able, whether directly or indirectly and whether
     or not that person is charged a fee, to:
       (a) invoke it, issue a command to it, or otherwise cause it to act;
       (b) interact with it or with any interface it presents; or
       (c) receive, view, or otherwise obtain its output.
     Adding the Software or a Modification to any Discord server, guild,
     channel, group, or account of which You are not the only member or user
     constitutes Deployment. Installing it as a Discord user-installed
     application on any account other than Your own constitutes Deployment.

1.9  "Permitted Local Use" means running the Software or a Modification solely
     on hardware or a hosted environment that You control, where You are the
     only person able to invoke it, interact with it, or receive its output,
     and solely for one or more of the Permitted Purposes.

1.10 "Permitted Purposes" means, and is limited to:
       (a) reading, studying, and understanding the Software;
       (b) evaluating the Software's quality, correctness, or behavior;
       (c) good-faith security research, vulnerability discovery, and testing;
       (d) preparing, developing, and testing a Contribution; and
       (e) academic study, teaching, or private non-commercial learning.

1.11 "Contribution" means any code, documentation, data, translation, design,
     bug report, test, or other material that You intentionally submit to the
     Licensor for inclusion in the Software, by any means, including a pull
     request, an issue, a message, or an email.

1.12 "Competing Service" means any bot, application, website, API, service, or
     product that provides, in whole or in substantial part, functionality
     comparable to that of the Software or the Official Service, whether or not
     it is offered for a fee, and whether or not it is directed at the same
     game, platform, or audience.

1.13 "AI/ML System" means any machine learning model, neural network, large
     language model, embedding index, retrieval corpus, or other automated
     system that is trained on, fine-tuned on, indexed over, or otherwise
     derives statistical or generative capability from input data.


